Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4fd6cc74-4fe1-d549-9095-de3469882d0c"],

Cell["\<\
If a variable is not initialized (as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]a\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is 1 at the beginning), it starts with the lowest \
value by default.

>With just c plot just changes its offset.
>When only b varies, the trajectory of minima seems to be parabolic. 
Plotting the function only varying b:
(value of the function at minima)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9457355210246315`*^9, 3.9457355829682903`*^9}, {
  3.9457356563605614`*^9, 3.945735715626583*^9}, {3.9457359135709896`*^9, 
