Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Population Growth",
  FontSize->24],
 "\nPopulation of a particular species (say bacteria) in an environment \
(assuming only that exists)\nN(t) - Population at time t\nr - growth rate\nK \
- carrying capacity\n\nI shall keep x instead of N since N is some predefined \
object in mathematica.\nSimplest model: dN/dt = rN\nThis suggests  N(t)=N0 \
exp(rt)\nHowever, there\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a certain carrying capacity above \
which, the population won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t grow.\n\nAnother model [Logistic \
equation]\ndN/dt = rN(1-(N/K))\nif N>K rate is negative."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9463439668287773`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"aad921ba-bb1f-1a40-ba03-\
36479f8bda72"],

